```js
async function runReportJob(job) {
  const depots = await db.depot.findMany();
  for (const depot of depots) {
    await sendReport(depot);
  }
  await db.reportJob.update({ where: { id: job.id }, data: { state: 'succeeded' } });
}
```

The worker was recycled while depot 10 of 12 was sending. The job's lease expired, it was re-queued, and a second worker ran it. Depots 1 to 9 received two reports.

What is the fix?

solution.explanationMarkdown:
The job records nothing until all twelve sends complete, so an interrupted run leaves no trace of the nine that succeeded. The rerun has no way to know, and repeats them.

Making each depot its own committed unit fixes it:

```js
const claimed = await db.reportDelivery.createMany({
  data: [{ jobId: job.id, depotId: depot.id }],
  skipDuplicates: true,        // UNIQUE (job_id, depot_id)
});
if (claimed.count === 0) continue;
await sendReport(depot, { idempotencyKey: `${job.id}:${depot.id}` });
```

A rerun now skips the nine that are recorded. The idempotency key covers the one remaining uncertainty — depot 10, which may have been sent before the crash — by making the provider responsible for that duplicate.

Note that no arrangement of local code closes that last window on its own: the send happens in someone else's system and cannot participate in your transaction. You can only shrink the window, and then decide which way it should fail.

solution.code:
function recoverStalled(jobs, now, leaseMs) {
  const requeue = [];
  const dead = [];
  const ignored = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < jobs.length; i += 1) {
    const job = jobs[i];
    if (job.state !== 'running') {
      ignored.push(job.id);
      continue;
    }
    let stalled = false;
    if (job.heartbeatAt === null || job.heartbeatAt === undefined) {
      stalled = true;
    } else if (now - job.heartbeatAt > leaseMs) {
      stalled = true;
    }
    if (!stalled) {
      ignored.push(job.id);
      continue;
    }
    if (job.attempts >= job.maxAttempts) {
      dead.push(job.id);
    } else {
      requeue.push(job.id);
    }
  }
  return { requeue: requeue, dead: dead, ignored: ignored };
}

